# SNIP architecture (this repository)

This repo is the first **SNIP domain application** (Network Planning & Optimisation), not the entire Simba Network Intelligence Platform.

Read before changing code:

- `docs/implementation/SNIP-IMPLEMENTATION-CONTEXT.md` (section 0 is authoritative for scope)
- `docs/implementation/SNIP-IMPLEMENTATION-STATUS.md`
- `docs/architecture/SNIP-PHASE-5-AGENTIC-ORCHESTRATION-CONTROLLED-AUTONOMY-ARCHITECTURE.md`
- `docs/implementation/SNIP-PHASE-5-AGENTIC-ORCHESTRATION-CONTROLLED-AUTONOMY-SPECIFICATION.md`

Root copies also exist:

- `SNIP-PHASE-5-AGENTIC-ORCHESTRATION-CONTROLLED-AUTONOMY-ARCHITECTURE.md`
- `SNIP-PHASE-5-AGENTIC-ORCHESTRATION-CONTROLLED-AUTONOMY-SPECIFICATION.md`

## Authorised now

Phase **5** is architecturally accepted and **frozen** on the Phase 4 baseline (`58c6e4111e83ef32137f2c0ffd083a060bd73796`). Do not add Phase 5 functionality, resolve deferred technical debt, or refactor for its own sake.

Preserve Phase 1A/1A.1/1B/2/3/4/5. Kafka remains off by default. Do not vectorize operational telemetry or Assurance Case state. Detection remains deterministic. The LLM explains and prioritises investigation; it does not decide thresholds, severity, confidence, risk, or policy. AI may propose. Deterministic policy decides. Humans approve where required. MCP invokes only registered capabilities.

Exactly one Chief Orchestration Agent plus Knowledge, Context, Assurance, and Decision specialists. Communication is orchestrator-mediated. Orchestration is synchronous and bounded. Persist structured AgentPlan / PlanStep only; no hidden chain-of-thought. Memory is ephemeral Run Memory, concise Case Memory, and existing Enterprise Memory. Agent Registry is in-code. Permissions are explicit least privilege. One shared physical LLM initially; AgentModelResolver is retained; no heterogeneous model routing. Agents reuse Phase 4 ProposedAction. Phase 4 remains authoritative for risk, policy, approval, execution, MCP, and action audit. Agents have no direct MCP or network execution authority.

Same-JVM loopback JSON-RPC HTTP MCP remains accepted. Phase 4 POST APIs mutate SNIP governance state only. Agent-run POST APIs mutate SNIP orchestration state only. They do not authorise live network mutation. Failed-result row replacement remains deferred technical debt. Non-interruptible per-Agent timeout is accepted Phase 5 technical debt; preserve the future interruptible timeout / run watchdog requirement and do not redesign it in Phase 5.

Governance POST APIs mutate SNIP workflow state only. They must never write to the live network. Direct LLM-to-MCP invocation is prohibited. Direct Agent-to-MCP invocation is prohibited.

## Do not implement

Agent Factory, dynamic Agent creation, self-modifying Agents, persistent conversational memory, long-running or continuous background Agents, freeform Agent-to-Agent mesh, automatic remediation, Agent approval authority, policy override, production Agent identity federation, different physical models per Agent, automatic model routing, live OSS/NMS/EMS integrations, live gNB/network writes, Ericsson ENM / Nokia NetAct writes, incident-management / ITSM, Schema Registry, Avro, Protobuf, Flink, Spark, Kafka Streams, dedicated time-series DB, EKS/Kubernetes, Kong, ALB, ALICE, RL, ML anomaly detection, adaptive thresholds, forecasting, billing, Ionic, AWS lock-in, production IAM/OIDC, remote third-party MCP, vendor MCP adapters, production RF simulation, full Digital Twin execution, network rollback, Phase 6.

## Rules

- Extend Phase 1A/1B/2/3/4 abstractions. Do not rewrite the slice.
- Keep recommendation and domain APIs read-only for the network. Action execute/approve mutate SNIP governance state only. Agent-run POST APIs mutate SNIP orchestration state only.
- If retrieval is empty, do not fabricate citations or specialist evidence.
- Ordinary CI must not download large models. PostgreSQL via Testcontainers remains required. Kafka Testcontainers remains allowed.
- Implementation markdown lives under `docs/implementation/`. ADRs under `docs/architecture/adr/`.
- Architecture document has architectural authority. Implementation specification is the authorised execution scope.
- Do not push or establish a new Git baseline until the Phase 5 completion report has been reviewed and explicit architectural acceptance has been granted.
